Custom JSON Parsing
While the default functionality is often sufficient, there are times you need to
override it. While time.Time supports JSON fields in RFC 339 format out of
the box, you might have to deal with other time formats. We can handle this by
creating a new type that implements two interfaces, json.Marshaler and
json.Unmarshaler :
type RFC822ZTime struct {
time.Time
}
func (rt RFC822ZTime) MarshalJSON() ([]byte, error) {
out := rt.Time.Format(time.RFC822Z)
return []byte(`"` + out + `"`), nil
}
func (rt *RFC822ZTime) UnmarshalJSON(b []byte) error {
if string(b) == "null" {
return nil
}
t, err := time.Parse(`"`+time.RFC822Z+`"`, string(b))
if err != nil {
return err
}
*rt = RFC822ZTime{t}
return nil
}
