Cancelation
Imagine that you have a request that spawns several goroutines, each one calling
a different HTTP service. If one service returns an error that prevents you from
returning a valid result, there is no point in continuing to process the other
goroutines. In Go, this is called cancelation and the context provides the
mechanism for implementing this.
To create a cancellable context, use the context.WithCancel function. It
takes in a context.Context as a parameter and returns a
context.Context and a context.CancelFunc. The returned
context.Context is not the same context that was passed in to the function.

